#. Diagram label
msgid "Nothing to do"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:52
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Offer the card and land only on the owner's tap."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:38
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Read live, never from a stored copy: the open PRs (draft, head, mergeable, owed checks, open owner decisions), the queued and running runs with the age of the oldest, the latest main push run, and each PR owner's last push or comment."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:37
#. Diagram label
msgid "Read PRs, runner queue, main verdict and owners"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:88
#. Diagram label
msgid "Ready"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:64
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Ready PRs that stack land as a train through merge:guard."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:87
#. Diagram label
msgid "Saturated"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:44
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Saturated: queued runs are 60+ minutes old and nothing has landed, or the owner says the runners are full. Stalled: a PR owner has been silent for 2+ hours. Ready: a PR stacks with green owed CI. Otherwise nothing."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:51
#. Diagram label
msgid "Saturation meta-merge"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:89
#. Diagram label
msgid "Stalled"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:68
#. Diagram label
msgid "Stalled-agent triage"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:69
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Tell the owner, then take the stalled PR over."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:16
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The loop run by the agent that holds the merge-steward lane (actor merge-manager, skill merge-manager-watcher), which coordinates with the swarm siblings whenever a batch lands. Each wake reads the open PRs, the runner queue, main's verdict and the PR owners live, and routes to one sub-process. A wake with nothing to do ends with no message. Every merge on any route waits for the owner's own OK."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn:19
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The merge manager, holding the merge-steward role across one or more repositories. Each wake it reads the open PRs, the runner queue, main's verdict and who owns each PR, then routes to the process the queue needs (merge train, saturation meta-merge, stalled-agent takeover) or stays idle."
msgstr ""

